  "question": {
    "text": "If $a+b+c=0,|\\vec{a}|=3,|\\vec{b}|=5$ and $|\\vec{c}|=7$, then the angle between $\\vec{a}$ and $\\vec{b}$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "E9K8D",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\pi}{3}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "UtxDY",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\pi}{4}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "M6qIT",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\pi}{6}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "OxUbr",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\pi}{2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let $a+b+c=0 \\Rightarrow(a+b)=-c$ $\\Rightarrow(a+b)^2=c^2$\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\Rightarrow a^2+b^2+2 a \\cdot b=c^2 \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow 9+25+2.3 .5 \\cos \\theta=49 \\\\\n& (\\because|\\vec{a}|=3,|\\vec{b}|=5 \\text { and }|\\vec{c}|=7) \\\\\n& \\therefore \\cos \\theta=\\frac{1}{2} \\Rightarrow \\theta=\\frac{\\pi}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
